---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const internal = (segment) => `${base}/${segment.replace(/^\//, '')}`;
const programmes = [
  {
    n: '01',
    title: 'Epistemic stewardship',
    copy: 'How should authority, accountability and authorship work when machine cognition can produce artefacts more sophisticated than their human curators can fully defend?',
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    title: 'Epistemic handoff & uptake',
    copy: 'How can valuable ideas from low-authority initiators be preserved, routed toward capable stewards and developed without confusing originator credit with epistemic authority?',
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    title: 'Agalmic economics',
    copy: 'What happens to value and allocation when useful knowledge, computation and other non-rival goods become dramatically cheaper to create?',
  },
  {
    n: '04',
    title: 'Epistemic economics',
    copy: 'When candidate knowledge is abundant, attention, validation, trust, interpretation and institutional capacity become the binding constraints.',
  },
  {
    n: '05',
    title: 'Innovation as search',
    copy: 'Innovation can be modelled as search across adjacent possibles, with machine cognition expanding exploration and humans choosing what to test, build and adopt.',
  },
  {
    n: '06',
    title: 'Coordination after abundance',
    copy: 'More possibilities do not remove choice. They intensify the problem of deciding what deserves scarce time, capital, legitimacy and physical resources.',
  },
  {
    n: '07',
    title: 'Representation as discovery',
    copy: 'How can systems compress, transform and embody information more cheaply while preserving the structure humans need to perceive what matters?',
  },
  {
    n: '08',
    title: 'Knowledge, property and rents',
    copy: 'How should publication, defensive disclosure, patents and incentives change when the cost of generating potentially valuable ideas collapses?',
  },
];
---
<Layout>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Economics after scarcity moves</p>
      <h1>When ideas become cheap, what becomes scarce?</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Agalmic Research studies economies in which machine cognition makes the generation of candidate knowledge abundant. The bottleneck moves toward attention, validation, coordination, trust, embodiment and the capacity to turn possibilities into reality.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href={internal('research')}>Explore the programme</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={internal('publications')}>Publication track</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Epistemic status</p>
        <h2>The programme begins by stating its own constraint.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">Machine cognition can increase the sophistication of an artefact faster than it increases the understanding of the human publishing it.</p>
        <p>Agalmic Research is extensively machine-assisted. Its public work should therefore not be read as evidence that the human curator possesses expert mastery of every field or argument involved. Publication establishes provenance and invites criticism; it does not certify mastery.</p>
        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>Epistemic authority should not exceed defensibility.</strong></p>
        </div>
        <p><a href={internal('publications/authorial-capacity-constraint')}>Read Working Paper 001: The Authorial Capacity Constraint →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Epistemic handoff</p>
        <h2>A good idea can outrun the expertise of the person who found it.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">The right response is neither false authority nor dismissal.</p>
        <p>An initiator may make a genuine contribution while lacking the domain authority needed to judge it. Agalmic Research therefore separates contribution provenance from epistemic authority and asks how candidate knowledge can be handed to capable framers, domain stewards, verifiers and realizers while preserving its origin.</p>
        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>Origin deserves credit. Authority requires warrant.</strong></p>
        </div>
        <p><a href={internal('drafts/epistemic-handoff')}>Read the Epistemic Handoff draft →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell thesis">
      <p class="eyebrow">Working thesis · The law of displaced scarcity</p>
      <blockquote>
        As one constraint becomes abundant, value migrates toward the complementary constraints required to select, verify, coordinate and realise it.
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        This is not a claim that scarcity disappears. It is a programme for tracing where scarcity goes next, and how institutions should change when the old bottleneck no longer explains the system.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Research programme</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>A field, not a single paper.</h2>
          <p>The programme begins with the epistemic conditions of machine-amplified research itself, then asks how promising knowledge is absorbed and where scarcity, value and institutional pressure move as cognitive production becomes abundant.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        {programmes.map((item) => (
          <article class="card">
            <span class="card-kicker">{item.n}</span>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.copy}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">No AGI threshold required</p>
        <h2>The transition can be studied now.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">Agalmic abundance is not a wager on a single future intelligence event.</p>
        <p class="muted">
          Cheap machine cognition already changes the economics of search, drafting, modelling and software creation. The research question is what happens when generation accelerates faster than our ability to evaluate, understand, route, coordinate and realise the resulting possibilities.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Applied research</p>
        <h2>Nemosyne as a testbed.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">The arguments should survive contact with software.</p>
        <p class="muted">
          <a href="https://nemosyne.world">nemosyne.world</a> explores a practical version of the same problem: how to choose representations that make meaningful structure perceptible without spending more computation, complexity or human attention than necessary. Its Moneta research direction treats representation as a constrained discovery problem rather than decoration.
        </p>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/nemosyne">Explore Nemosyne on GitHub ↗</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Operating model</p>
        <h2>Publish early. State epistemic status. Preserve provenance. Hand off intelligently.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Research begins as a canonical, versioned object. From that source it can become a working paper, journal article, public essay, policy brief, talk, model or piece of software without pretending that one format is the research itself.
        </p>
        <div class="callout">
          <p>Publication is part of the research method: establish provenance, expose ideas to criticism, make reuse cheap and let better arguments compound. Openness does not remove the obligation to state what is understood, what is verified, who contributed what and where further expertise is needed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href={internal('principles')}>Read the principles</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={internal('drafts')}>Browse drafts</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
